<DocLayout title="Changelog" eyebrow="Project continuity" description="A concise record of user-visible changes, implementation milestones, and research-status updates." next={{ label: "Contribute", href: "/contributing/" }}>
  <h2>Current direction</h2>
  <p>The project is prioritizing a usable public product surface: native documentation, developer onboarding, a clear mode contract, and honest release boundaries.</p>
  <h2>Product surface</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Added native routes for getting started, the playground, concepts, modes, API reference, examples, architecture, research status, and contribution guidance.</li>
    <li>Added an interactive matching model with keyboard operation, screen-reader announcements, and metric explanations.</li>
    <li>Made the first-use path executable in CI, including installation, updates, matching inspection, partner lookup, statistics, and maximality checks.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Engineering boundary</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Canonicalized the public API around <code>basic</code> and <code>multilevel</code>; legacy names and compatibility wrappers are not supported.</li>
    <li>Added atomic update validation and rollback-safe state exposure across graph, matching, index, and hierarchy state.</li>
    <li>Hardened recursive schedules, graph identity, deferred deletion checks, and deterministic verification.</li>
    <li><code>basic</code> is the recommended integration path. <code>multilevel</code> remains available for research and evaluation while full paper-level guarantees are validated.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For source-level history, use the repository as an engineering reference after starting with the public documentation.</p>
</DocLayout>
